From 9d1482d4e677b50eadfb4cc85825f1a0252c1db6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:05:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: describe the review or the machine, not session codes
 or host names

Comments and docstrings in 62 test files named the review sessions that
measured something (by their codes) or the machines a measurement was made
on (by their host names). Each now says what the reader needs: the review
it came from ("the #1225 review", "review round 3"), or the kind of machine
where it matters ("a 96-thread Linux workstation", "a Linux cluster", "a
workstation"). Where neither matters the attribution is dropped.

Text only: with docstrings dropped and every string constant replaced by a
placeholder, each file's AST is identical before and after. One string
constant changes, a dictionary key in test_1134 whose values alone are read.
The six files the docstring branch for UNFILED 57 edits are left to it.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
